Author:     Ben Campbell <benc@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Tue Apr 7 20:56:20 2026 +0000
Commit:     Ben Campbell <benc@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Tue Apr 7 20:56:20 2026 +0000

    Bug 1806770 - Add a ImapUid type, and have all XPCOM interfaces use it when passing IMAP UIDs. r=mkmelin


    This adds the ImapUid typedef via ImapTypes.idl, and changes all the other
    IMAP IDL files to use it instead of uint32_t or (worse) nsMsgKey.

    This just makes sure the XPCOM interfaces are really clear on which parameters
    are UIDs and which are nsMsgKey, even if they are still interchangable in the
    underlying code.

    As a general rule of thumb, nsIImapProtocol and it's helpers should deal
    exclusively with UIDs, while everywhere else (i.e. the folder side of the
    folder/protocol boundary) else should use database keys (nsMsgKey), only
    mapping them to/from UIDs when talking to the protocol side.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291677

diff --git a/mailnews/imap/public/ImapTypes.idl b/mailnews/imap/public/ImapTypes.idl
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..1885a18d563
--- /dev/null
+++ b/mailnews/imap/public/ImapTypes.idl
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+/* This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+ * License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+ * file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/. */
+
+#include "nsISupports.idl"
+
+/**
+ * Type for IMAP UIDs.
+ * Also used for sequence numbers, on particularly backward servers.
+ * Ideally this typedef would prevent accidental casting to/from uint32_t and
+ * (especially) nsMsgKey, but there doesn't seem to be a simple way to enforce
+ * that with XPCOM.
+ */
+typedef unsigned long ImapUid;
+
+
+%{C++
+// This should be 0 (unused by IMAP), but we currently need to be
+// interchangable with nsMsgKey.
+constexpr ImapUid ImapUid_None = 0xffffffff;
+%}
